Files derived from other projects
---------------------------------

mod/probe.S
    Derived from dnfw (angellinares/dn2_firmware_explore), csrc/usbprobe/probe.S, AGPL-3.0-or-later, which is
    derived from irpina/digihealth (sysinfo.s), GPL-2.0-or-later.

tools/dgprobe.py
    Protocol and codec derived from dnfw, tools/dn2probe.py, AGPL-3.0-or-later, which is derived from
    irpina/digihealth (tools/digiusb.py), GPL-2.0-or-later.

mod/preflight.py
    The rules of dnfw v0.50's safety check, applied to the stock file of the OS being built. Calls dnfw.

port/harness_1.12.patch
    Local changes to two other projects, kept as a patch with a few lines of their context:
    complex-ping/digitone-2-modding-skill, scripts/cfkit.py (MIT), and m-dwyer/digikit,
    devices/digitone-ii.toml (GPL-2.0-or-later).

model/digiglide.py, mod/core/dg_core.c
    The glide planner, voice leading, paths, Moves and tables are a port of Brickglide, part of
    michaeltietjen/brickchord (brickchord/ambient.py, engine.py, main.py), MIT, by the same author.

Used at build or test time, not included
----------------------------------------

dnfw (angellinares/dn2_firmware_explore), AGPL-3.0-or-later
    Firmware container and signing, the runtime loader (csrc/runtime/loader.S, built into every image), the code
    area, the parameter table relocation (dnfw.patch.paramtable), verification. A built DigiGlide image therefore
    contains dnfw code, which is why DigiGlide is AGPL-3.0-or-later.

digitone-2-modding-skill (complex-ping), MIT
    The ColdFire build helpers and the emulator harness the tests drive (cfmod, cfkit, emu).

digikit (m-dwyer), GPL-2.0-or-later, and digiemu (irpina), GPL-2.0-or-later
    The emulators (ColdFire and SHARC) the tests run in.

Read, no code taken
-------------------

naturarum/dn2-cfw (Digiwerk), GPL-2.0: its notes on the kit record, the kit serializer and the parameter table
(T6.0, T6.3, docs/parameter-table-growth.md) guided where DigiGlide keeps its settings. Addresses and layouts
were checked against the author's own OS 1.12 file and unit.
